Package: zuroar
Title: Compressed Sets of Unsigned Integers with 'Roaring' Bitmaps
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("The CRoaring authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "CRoaring, bundled in src/croaring; see inst/COPYRIGHTS"))
Description: Compressed sets of unsigned integers from 0 to 2^32 - 1, and
    up to 2^64 - 1, built on a bundled copy of 'CRoaring', the reference C
    implementation of 'Roaring' bitmaps (Lemire et al. 2018
    <doi:10.1002/spe.2560>). A bitmap answers membership, cardinality,
    rank, select and the set operations without materialising a vector,
    and serialises to the portable 'Roaring' format shared by
    implementations in 'Java', 'Go', 'Rust' and 'Python'. To R code a
    bitmap behaves as a sorted vector without duplicates.
